  ⚠️  samples/s could NOT be recovered for the 1 Hz round. The quantum is found as
      gcd(twin readings), which needs the readings to be multiples of one sample:
      1 kHz  (2026-08-20):   24 distinct non-zero readings, gcd = 11,812,864  <- quantised, recovery valid
      1 Hz   (2026-09-01):  559 distinct non-zero readings, gcd = 1  <- NOT quantised, recovery INVALID
      Traffic equality is therefore established above on packets and tx bytes,
      which need no quantum. The kernel CPU figures below are unaffected either
      way -- they come from /proc/<pid>/stat and never touch the twin.

