================================================================================================
IS THE DIFFERENCE A CONSTANT OFFSET?
================================================================================================
  The recompute thread does not touch the ingest path, so IF the difference were
  that change, it should sit at the same size on every sampling rate. A delta that
  grows with the sample rate is something else -- or something else as well.

  poll-off deltas: -46.2, -46.5, -45.9, -46.3, -46.6
  mean -46.28   spread (max-min) 0.68

================================================================================================
🔴 WHAT THIS IS NOT
================================================================================================
  The 08-20 round ran on a kernel twelve days older: ticket Q's in-loop divisor
  instrument and the B-2(1)/E-2 fixes all landed in between, and no one-constant-
  apart binary was built. Every delta above is the difference between two ROUNDS.
  It is not the effect of 1 kHz -> 1 Hz, and must not be reported as one.
